      "content": "Teaching only about mistakes and systemic problems without acknowledging human agency and progress actually breeds the cynicism you fear, not the critical thinking you want. A curriculum that balances historical struggles with the resilience of the people who overcame them creates a more robust sense of identity than one that focuses solely on triumphs or solely on grievances. This approach empowers students to understand that society is dynamic and can be improved, which is far more effective for their development than leaving them with a hopeless or artificially positive narrative.",
